{title: I Sing the Mighty Power of God}
{artist: Isaac Watts}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
I [D]sing the mighty [G]power of [D]God that [G]made the [D]mountains [A]rise,
that [D]spread the flowing [G]seas a[D]broad and [G]built the [D]lofty [A]skies.
I [D]sing the wisdom [A]that or[Bm]dained the [D]sun to [A]rule the [D]day;
the [D]moon shines full at [G]his com[D]mand, and [G]all the [D]stars o[A]bey.

Verse 2
I [D]sing the goodness [G]of the [D]Lord, That filled [G]the earth [D]with [A]food:
He [D]formed the creatures [G]with His word, [G]And then [D]pronounced [A]them
good. [D]Lord, how Thy [A]wonders are displayed, [D]Where'er I [A]turn my [D]eye;
If [D]I survey the ground [G]I tread, Or [G]gaze upon [D]the sky.

Verse 3
There's [D]not a plant [G]or flow'r [D]below, But [G]makes Thy [D]glories [A]known;
And [D]clouds arise and [G]tempests blow, By [G]order from [D]Thy [A]throne.
Creatures [D]that borrow life [A]from Thee Are [D]subject to [A]Thy care: [D]There's
not [D]a place where we [G]can flee, But [G]God is [D]present there.
